<title>LATVIA: TRADE DEFICIT Q1 FALLS TO 111.4 MLN LATS.</title>
<headline>TRADE DEFICIT Q1 FALLS TO 111.4 MLN LATS.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's first quarter trade deficit fell to 111.4 million lats compared with 112.2 million lats in the first quarter of 1996, the statistics committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee gave the figures in real prices, which do not take inflation into account. Annual inflation in April was 8.8 percent.  </p>
<p>Figures are in millions of lats unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>LATVIAN TRADE BALLANCE  Jan-March '97 Jan-Feb '97 Jan-March'96</p>
<p> Exports		     209.74	   99.9	175.07</p>
<p> Imports		     321.09	  108.8	287.27</p>
<p> Balance		     -111.4	  -72.03     -112.2</p>
<p>Principal trading partners:</p>
<p>Exports Q1 1997 vs Q1 1996 (percentage of the total):</p>
<p>Russia  - 20.9 vs 26.6</p>
<p>Britain - 15.8 vs  9.4</p>
<p>Germany - 14.1 vs 14.1</p>
<p>Imports Q1 1997 vs Q1 1996 (percentage of the total):</p>
<p>Russia  - 18.6 vs 22.7</p>
<p>Germany - 14.1 vs 13.3</p>
<p>Finland -  9.5 vs  9.0</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
